{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1553559-god-level-enemies","id":1553559,"title":"God level enemies","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-08-30T15:44:10-07:00","id":1553559,"title":"God level enemies","content":"How do you as a ST play battle encounters with god level enemies like a talon of the wyrm or a greater incana spirit vs player mages? Anyone has experience with this kind of play?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-30T19:56:00-07:00","id":1553560,"title":"","content":"Try this idea. A time traveler who is heroic, good at heart, but has a serious flaw. The Traveler wants to make history &quot;better.&quot; But, although the Traveler is noble and pure hearted, they have a messed up few of history. <br /> <br /> Remember Capaldi's line as the 12th Doctor. &quot;You'll find the universe is a small place when I'm angry at you.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-31T01:41:06-07:00","id":1553562,"title":"","content":"Unless I am doing a game about arch-mages, I tend to treat things of that scale as plot devices the characters role play around rather than something with stats they fight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-31T07:06:08-07:00","id":1553564,"title":"","content":"You don't actually need to get to god level enemies to have brutally one-sided battles in Mage, either in favor of your PCs or against them. If the game is going well, brutally one-sided battles are the norm the more powerful everyone gets.<br /> <br /> As a rule of thumb the game is ultimately, in its aspect as a game, about preparedness and creativity. When a decisive battle begins in Mage, it's result is already written by whatever the PCs did beforehand. Improvised spells may play a role, but they won't be enough to make it against any serious opposition of a &quot;higher level&quot;. PCs need data, rituals, carefully chosen countermeasures and weapons.<br /> <br /> Remember: Spirits and Night-folk aren't only intelligent beings able to stack odds in their favor, when it comes to natural advantages they're ahead of Mages by a large margin. It's similar to fighting someone that already has a dozen or more spells cast beforehand, and on top of that higher dice-pools. If the PCs don't have the right answers for those, they're going to get steamrolled and that's it.<br /> <br /> Now, some advice that works for me most of the time:<br /> <br /> 1- Don't make the battle an end in itself. Each party in it has one or more goals, and attaining those goals only tangentially requires confrontation. That means neither side has to kill the other to achieve their goals, and that's the simpler way to &quot;balance&quot; an asymmetrical confrontation. Buying time, reaching point B, destroying or protecting a third party or object, there are several ways to make the battle something else. That way your PCs don't have to overpower something impossible or nearly impossible, and if the enemy wins they don't have to obliterate the party, the PCs live to continue their story;<br /> <br /> 2- Pay extra attention to what your PCs do to prepare for what they'll face. Give them the time and opportunity to find out what they'll face and what it can do, and to think how they can face those problems. Have at least one &quot;correct answer&quot; prepared, a step-by-step plan using resources they have that will have a good chance of succeeding given mostly average rolls and some room for failure. You don't ever have to disclose this plan or anything, it's just a proof-of-concept to be sure they're up to the challenge, they'll probably do something else entirely;<br /> <br /> 3- Focus on making this preparation the bulk of the &quot;battle&quot;. Let them stack as much advantages as possible, and nudge them to do so if they seem too confident too soon. Turn any idea on how to get an edge into a quest. Let them travel, explore, make alliances, try what seems impossible. Give them plenty of informants and advisors that can direct them to the things they want to try, how to try and so on. You can also use such informants to throw any ideas you have yourself, whether you think they're feasible or not, just to keep thoughts running;<br /> <br /> 4- Learn aspects of the game you usually don't use in your games. Wonders, Ritual Casting, all kinds of Spirits, Bygones, Crafts, Sorcerers, anything at all, and help your players towards how to use and benefit from that thing. The road to fighting a god is the moment to really do a little of everything and try new things. It's also time to explore ways towards those things you don't usually go through, from searching legendary Wonders in ancient ruins to making contracts with mercenary Extraordinary Citizens trained to do battle in weird Reality Zones. Get Nightfolk involved that may help in some way, either by using their simplified stats in Mage or learning their own gamelines;<br /> <br /> 5- Give the opponent a weakness, mechanical or not. Something they want or have to protect, but can't give it full attention. Materials or actions that affect them beyond the normal rules, like causing immense damage, disabling powers, reducing dice-pools or otherwise hampering their capacity to operate at full power. A greater danger they have to be careful not to attract. Anything that can either act as a powerful attack or debuff, or that limits or controls the actions of the enemy. This can either be the centerpiece of the battle, or just a final option if something goes wrong and you want to tip the balance in the PCs favor without an actual <i>Deus-Ex-Machina</i>;<br /> <br /> 6- Enjoy the road, not the finish line. The battle has to be a dramatic climax for the story, but not the challenge itself. If things get balanced enough for victory to seem uncertain and the battle move back and forth for some rounds, that's wonderful, but be prepared to have everything sorted out much sooner for either side and the descriptions and exchanges make for the drama in lieu of the dice. Such a battle is just too unpredictable for you to rely too much on the system doing the talking.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-31T07:41:34-07:00","id":1553565,"title":"","content":"To be frank i want to do an equivalent of the battle agains the Storm Eater but for mages not werewolves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-31T08:19:49-07:00","id":1553566,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1553559-god-level-enemies?p=1553565#post1553565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be frank i want to do an equivalent of the battle agains the Storm Eater but for mages not werewolves.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing is, they're Mages, not Werewolves.<br /> <br /> Werewolves at high levels have immense dice pools, sometimes literally dozens of dice, a lot of passive benefits of all kinds as Gifts and Totem, possibly a lot of spirit allies to help in battle, they have Fetishes they make with far more ease to add to their capabilities, they're extremely hard to harm significantly for long even before adding defensive effects and items, not to say their many ways of keeping synergy within the group, so the Pack is, indeed, more than the sum of its parts in a way no other splat does, much less Mage, and they have all that without any preparation whatsoever.<br /> <br /> It's a whole 'nother game. The only way to have a Werewolf-like battle in Mage is if the PCs decide on their own that they want to battle like Werewolves. It is doable for them to prepare by ritual casting buffs and defenses and stacking effects so they end up as combat machines. But that's strictly on the players, not on you, and is still more unpredictable, with a higher risk of things simply not playing out as you envision.<br /> <br /> Mage is not Werewolf. Mage players have a lot of agency on how they'll deal with anything they face, the system actively rewards lateral thinking, and they have frail bodies without any of the advantages of a Werewolf (the single most buffed-up splat in the game by far other than Fera) or natural defense against absolute, unrestricted violence. They're literally as weak as any human, and their single real strength is their unlimited capacity to make shit up <b><u>when they prepare</u></b>.<br /> <br /> Simply put, if you run a Mage game as a Werewolf game and pit them against Storm Eater, they'll TPK. They'll TPK against far weaker foes. And I'm assuming Arete 10 Archmages, they'll simply die horribly and fast.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-31T09:45:12-07:00","id":1553567,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1553559-god-level-enemies?p=1553566#post1553566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The thing is, they're Mages, not Werewolves.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly, advanced mages will wipe the floor with any werewolf pack. With preparation (or even just standard paranoja preparation daily defences) they win 10 out of 10 times so it should be easier for mages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-31T16:43:33-07:00","id":1553571,"title":"","content":"A good enemy for a Mage would be like a good enemy for Superman. Someone who can negate the advantages of the mages. Mages aren't good at time travel, so a time traveler is a major threat. Conspiracies of ordinary mortals like the Mafia or some intelligence agency that sees Mages as a threat are very hard to see coming and can make the Mages outcasts. Religious organizations, even if they don't have the resources of the Society of Leopold, can be major threats. Other mages, even if they aren't as powerful, can leverage inside knowledge and social connections to hurt the PCs.<br /> <br /> Remember, stronger than anybody isn't equal to stronger than everybody. Similarly, smarter than anybody isn't smarter than everybody.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 02-08-2026, 02:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-01T02:52:54-07:00","id":1553575,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1553559-god-level-enemies?p=1553565#post1553565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be frank i want to do an equivalent of the battle agains the Storm Eater but for mages not werewolves.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then do so. 2nd Edition Mage started with a space and ground battle on Mercury. Mage is very capable of doing large scale events.<br /> <br /> You don't even need Archmages, Master Mages themselves can do things like nuclear scale attacks and shields against nuclear scale attacks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27335-technoma","name":"Technoma","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-01T02:56:57-07:00","id":1553576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Technoma</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1553559-god-level-enemies?p=1553575#post1553575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Then do so. 2nd Edition Mage started with a space and ground battle on Mercury. Mage is very capable of doing large scale events.<br /> <br /> You don't even need Archmages, Master Mages themselves can do things like nuclear scale attacks and shields against nuclear scale attacks.</div> </div> </div> </div>I intend to, lookig on advice on how to do something on this scale.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-06T10:00:00-07:00","id":1553672,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1553559-god-level-enemies?p=1553567#post1553567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Exactly, advanced mages will wipe the floor with any werewolf pack. With preparation (or even just standard paranoja preparation daily defences) they win 10 out of 10 times so it should be easier for mages.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a bold statement to make, for all the reasons monteparnas mentioned above, and the endless nerfing of mages. <br /> <br /> To be fair, I don't think even werewolves are that well-suited to battle enemies on that level. The Storm Eater was defeated by a ritual with a very high cost. The ritual to stop the Eater of Souls demanded the sacrifice of an entire tribe. It wasn't just werewolves showing up for a smackdown.<br /> <br /> And as everyone else pointed out, mages in WoD are the runts of the litter. They're sneaky and versatile; they're not meant to Godmode through a battlefield.<br /> <br /> So given that a) mages are super squishy, b) true magic is, in fact, pretty weak, especially compared to other splats and c) as previously mentioned, mages require a lot of prep to do their thing somewhat efficiently, if you want a spectacular battle scene, it might be doable, but you have your work cut out for you.<br /> <br /> Aside from stocking up on wonders, my best suggestion to fight a god might be replicating the DnD &quot;memorized spells&quot; approach with archmages using Time 4. Your archmages could prepare a lot of powerful effects as rituals ahead of time, and activate them as needed with triggers. One of these should ideally be a variation of <u>The Shiva/Kali Murder Machine</u> to buff you up for at least a scene to help mitigate your human squishiness.<br /> <br /> I've never run or played the final boss fight with Voormas in Ascension, but it seems that is the closest canon scenario to what you're trying to do, so maybe check to see if there is anything there that you could adapt ?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26426-trianoma4evah","name":"Trianoma4Evah","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-06T22:23:10-08:00","id":1558156,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1553559-god-level-enemies?p=1553567#post1553567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Exactly, advanced mages will wipe the floor with any werewolf pack. With preparation (or even just standard paranoja preparation daily defences) they win 10 out of 10 times so it should be easier for mages.</div> </div> </div> </div>You've got vampires out here cursing / nuking entire bloodlines with their watered down blood sorcery. A fully Awakened mage with access to true magic is not somebody to be fucked around with.<br /> <br /> <br /> That being said, finding ways to achieve the impossible and kill enemies you have no reasonable business fighting is something that table top role players are infamously skilled at. If the players look at a Nexus Crawler and think to themselves <i>&quot;nah, I'd win.&quot;</i> - I think I'd be curious just to see how it plays out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-07T16:02:50-08:00","id":1558166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1553559-god-level-enemies?p=1558156#post1558156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You've got vampires out here cursing / nuking entire bloodlines with their watered down blood sorcery. A fully Awakened mage with access to true magic is not somebody to be fucked around with.<br /> <br /> <br /> That being said, finding ways to achieve the impossible and kill enemies you have no reasonable business fighting is something that table top role players are infamously skilled at. If the players look at a Nexus Crawler and think to themselves <i>&quot;nah, I'd win.&quot;</i> - I think I'd be curious just to see how it plays out.</div> </div> </div> </div>A nexus crawler (at least the stated one from the books) is kinda weak. Yes he has reality manipulation but he can do that once a turn and has only 7 dice for it with a high difficulty for the good stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-07T18:04:39-08:00","id":1558173,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1553559-god-level-enemies?p=1558166#post1558166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A nexus crawler (at least the stated one from the books) is kinda weak. Yes he has reality manipulation but he can do that once a turn and has only 7 dice for it with a high difficulty for the good stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>&quot;I turn your flesh to cotton, and your skin to velvet. Your pack of werewolves are now a bunch of plushies!&quot;</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-08T12:05:40-08:00","id":1558188,"title":"","content":"Mages versus Werewolves has a similarity to Batman versus Superman. Given time to prepare and solid intelligence a high level Mage has a serious advantage over a Werewolf pack. However, take away preparation time and Mages are at a disadvantage. Although a Master of Forces or Life could seriously ruin a Werewolf's day even on the fly. A conjuctive effect of Forces/Matter/Correspondence and Prime, sending molten silver through a Werewolf's bone marrow would finish a Werewolf quickly. But the Werewolf probably got done first.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 02-09-2026, 01:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-09T10:33:06-08:00","id":1558206,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1553559-god-level-enemies?p=1558173#post1558173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <i>&quot;I turn your flesh to cotton, and your skin to velvet. Your pack of werewolves are now a bunch of plushies!&quot;</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Good luck in getting 4 successes with 7 dificulty","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-09T14:58:40-08:00","id":1558211,"title":"","content":"Not counting exploding 10s, the probability of getting 4 successes at difficulty 7 is: <br /> <br /> Arete 4: 2.56%. <br /> Arete 5: 8.704%. <br /> Arete 6: 17.92%. <br /> Arete 7: 28.9792%.<br /> Arete 8: 40.59136%<br /> Arete 9: 51.7390336%<br /> <br /> \u2026and that's if you try to do it in just one roll. If you're willing to take your time and accumulate successes, 4 successes at difficulty 7 really isn't all that much of a problem; the issue ceases to be &quot;can they do it?&quot; and instead becomes &quot;how long will it take?&quot; Even at Arete 4, you should be able to accumulate enough successes for this in three rolls on average. <br /> <br /> Alternately, if you can come up with \u20133 difficulty worth of Magical Modifiers (such as using an instrument that you no longer need to use, or having something with an appropriate Resonance), you'll be attempting this feat at difficulty 4; and even at Arete 4, that's four successes in one roll 24% of the time. I'd have to crunch the numbers to be sure; but I suspect that even at Arete 5, you'd be more likely than not to pull it off immediately.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-10T20:44:58-08:00","id":1558223,"title":"","content":"If the Nexus Crawler has 7 dice to spend on reality warping, getting those 4 successes shouldn't be too hard to accomplish.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-17T02:43:31-08:00","id":1558361,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1553559-god-level-enemies?p=1558223#post1558223\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the Nexus Crawler has 7 dice to spend on reality warping, getting those 4 successes shouldn't be too hard to accomplish.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like stated above its less than 30% chance","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-17T23:24:36-07:00","id":1561874,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1553559-god-level-enemies?p=1558188#post1558188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mages versus Werewolves has a similarity to Batman versus Superman. Given time to prepare and solid intelligence a high level Mage has a serious advantage over a Werewolf pack. However, take away preparation time and Mages are at a disadvantage. Although a Master of Forces or Life could seriously ruin a Werewolf's day even on the fly. A conjuctive effect of Forces/Matter/Correspondence and Prime, sending molten silver through a Werewolf's bone marrow would finish a Werewolf quickly. But the Werewolf probably got done first.</div> </div> </div> </div>Basically what I meant.<br /> <br /> The problem with Mage is that battles aren't a challenge: one side will steamroll the other.<br /> <br /> If the Mages are prepared and competent, they win. If not, they die horribly.<br /> <br /> A Master could do a lot to a Werewolf in the fly, were it not for the Werewolf burning 2 Rage to auto-win initiative and make 3 attacks. At least something to counter that would be necessary preparation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}